// How the import normalizes source conventions.
//
// Mapping loss and quality. Every mapping
// carries at most one derived `effect` (common.kdl Effect: what the
// mapping does to the source's meaning beyond the relationship's
// direction) and one derived `quality` (0-100). Both are computed by
// the rubric below from the claim's published comment, so a comment
// that states a loss yields the loss in both fields; a mapping with no
// rubric input carries neither, so absent = not assessed. Equivalents
// with no loss stay plain `equivalent` with no effect.
//
// Rubric `mapping-quality@1` (deterministic; same comment -> same
// number). Inputs: the claim's relationship kind, its comment text,
// and — for lab-se -> npu claims — the NPU-part preservation fraction
// f (how many of the four NPU name parts — system, component,
// kind-of-property, specimen — the target spelling preserves). The
// NPU input is declared but yields no assignments while the legacy
// numeric target ids carry no derivable NPU full name. Where a
// comment class matches, the first hit by this priority wins — the
// loss classes rank first, so a comment that states a loss yields the
// loss in both fields and a verified basis never outranks a loss
// class:
//
//   1. hierarchy step  (the target called loose/broad/general/
//                       coarse within a short window of parent/
//                       target/concept)  effect=omitted quality=60
//   2. approximation   ("only parent", "no closer", "broad parent",
//                       "closest available", "closest match",
//                       "closest is", "not exact", "approxim*",
//                       "imprecise")     effect=omitted quality=40
//   3. lost facet      ("loss", "loses", "lost", "drops", "dropped",
//                       "omits", "omitted", "not preserved",
//                       "does not distinguish", "cannot distinguish",
//                       "does not separate", "cannot separate",
//                       "less specific")  effect=omitted quality=40
//                       — fires beside a verified basis (the
//                       loss-under-verified class: a stated loss never
//                       sits under a 100 stamp); a loss statement
//                       without a basis stays unassessed
//   4. verified        ("crosswalk-verified", "exact match",
//                       "dict-resident")             quality=100
//                       — reached only in the absence of a loss
//                       class. Loss language outside these classes
//                       falls to the residual rule 5.
//   5. residual loss   a verified basis standing beside loss
//                       language outside the classes above: a
//                       `granularity` hit ranks as a hierarchy step
//                       (effect=omitted, quality=60); any other hit
//                       (the loss-statement family) ranks as a lost
//                       facet (effect=omitted, quality=40)
//
// `effect=changed` and `effect=unknown` are never assigned
// mechanically: changed is curation-only, unknown marks unassessed
// claims if a consumer needs the explicit spelling.
// Relationship accuracy (mapping-consistency@1, deterministic; same
// inputs -> same kinds). After the source table above, a consistency
// pass reads each claim's published comment and its structured context
// (source and target system, endpoint id) and corrects confident
// mislabels; evidence without a confident act is left unchanged for
// human triage. Where a rule applies, the first hit by this priority
// wins:
//
//   1. direction contradiction: the comment's directional language
//      names the source or the target as the broader side; a kind
//      contradicting the described direction is rewritten (a declared
//      equivalent included; related_to never — it asserts no
//      direction, and its comments use direction words to argue for
//      relatedness). Conflicting subjects queue; subjectless direction
//      words on a single-claim equivalent queue; a standing verified
//      basis ("crosswalk-verified", "exact match", "dict-resident")
//      outranks an unattributable direction word.
//   2. site-vs-disease: the tree's ICD-O-3 codes are topography codes
//      (anatomical sites), so an equivalent to a disease-like SNOMED CT
//      target (disorder/finding/event/situation class, by the private
//      RF2 mirror's FSN tag or IS-A ancestry) is partial_overlap —
//      the concepts genuinely overlap but neither subsumes the other.
//      Targets the mirror cannot classify keep their kind and queue.
//   3. approximation: an equivalent whose published comment states an
//      approximation (closest/approximate/imprecise/not-exact family)
//      without a standing verified basis is partial_overlap.
//   4. namespace spell: a SNOMED CT target id in the Swedish-extension
//      partition (<digits>100005210<check>) names a SNOMED CT Swedish extension
//      concept, and the endpoint spells that namespace.
//   5. loss-under-verified: a verified basis standing beside loss
//      language the quality rubric's residual rule grades
//      (granularity 60, other loss statements 40) — relationships
//      stay untouched by that grading; the classified loss language
//      is already re-derived by the quality rubric.
//
score-scheme "vocabmod-se-confidence" version="1" kind=confidence direction=higher-is-better minimum=0 maximum=1 {
    description "en" "Derived mapping confidence, tier H/M/L, fitted on a 588-case training batch of blinded assessments under the documented assessment rubric and reported on a held-out 291-case sample. The score is the tier's Wilson 95% lower bound of exact agreement with the concept the blinded assessment accepts (training batch): 0.87 H, 0.71 M, 0.03 L. Signals: the target resolves in the local Athena release to an OMOP-standard concept, directly or through one valid Maps to, and BioLORD-2023-M (frozen dictionary) ranks that concept among the top-100 candidates for the source designation. H: rank 1 and top-1 score >= 0.85. M: rank 1 below that score, or rank 2-3. L: rank 4 or worse, including absent from the top 100 — the assessment presents only the top 10, so L's near-zero measured rate reflects that no independent signal corroborates the target, not that the target is wrong. The ICD-10-SE truncation path (icd10se-icd10cm-trunc) is capped at M. A score is a population rate over the tier, never a per-mapping probability, and the reference standard is blinded assessment under the documented rubric (first- and second-pass blind agreement about 81%), not expert clinical review."
}
score-scheme "vocabmod-se-confidence-unassessable" version="1" kind=confidence direction=unordered minimum=1 maximum=5 {
    description "en" "Explicit no-assessment marker for mappings that carry no confidence under vocabmod-se-confidence@1. The score is the reason: 1 target-not-standard (the target resolves in the local Athena release but is neither OMOP-standard nor one Maps to away from a standard concept), 2 target-outside-athena (the target system is not among the release's OMOP vocabularies), 3 target-unresolved (the target code is absent from the release), 4 source-designation-less (the source code has no designation text to retrieve with), 5 source-outside-population (the source is not one of the corpus's Swedish systems). Unassessable is a property of the evidence, never a verdict on the mapping."
}
score-scheme "mapping-quality" version="1" kind=quality direction=higher-is-better minimum=0 maximum=100 {
    description "en" "Derived mapping quality under rubric mapping-quality@1: 100 where the claim's comment states a verified or exact basis (crosswalk-verified, exact match, dict-resident) and states no loss class; 60 where the comment states a hierarchy step (the target called loose, broad, general or coarse near parent/target/concept) or, beside a verified basis, concedes a granularity loss; 40 where the comment states an approximation (only parent, no closer, broad parent, closest available/match/is, not exact, approximations, imprecision), a lost facet beside a verified basis (a named facet the target does not carry: the loss/loses/lost, drops/dropped, omits/omitted, not preserved, does not distinguish, does not separate, less specific family), or any other loss statement beside a verified basis — a stated loss never sits under a 100 stamp; absent where no class matches (not assessed). Each of the 60- and 40-band mappings pairs quality with effect=omitted."
}
translation-table "mapping-kind" version="1" source-column="maps_to_mapping_type" target-field="relationship" {
    description "en" "The source names the target's extent relative to the source."
    entry "exact_match" "equivalent"
    entry "broader" "source_is_narrower_than_target" note="the target is broader"
    entry "narrower" "source_is_broader_than_target" note="the target is narrower"
    entry "related" "related_to"
    entry "partial" "partial_overlap"
    entry "no_match" drop=#true note="Imported as a no-match assessment for the target system"
}
// SNOMED CT targets retired after a mapping was authored stay in place: a
// mapping records the standard concept that carried the source's
// meaning at authorship time, and a later retirement (invalid_reason
// D/U in a newer release) is a vocabulary life-cycle event, not
// evidence the mapping was wrong. Successors were looked up in Athena:
// where OHDSI publishes an unambiguous Maps-to replacement to an
// active standard SNOMED CT concept, the mapping retargets to that
// successor (applied for 10 of the 24 retired targets); the remaining
// 14 — 13 with no Athena successor, 1 ambiguous — stay in place as
// historical targets. The same successor bar applies to the
// 18 equivalent claims whose OMOP target ids turned invalid in the
// 2026-10-30 Athena download (12 unique ids, disjoint from the keep-set
// above): 10 targets (16 claims) retarget to the verified standard
// Maps-to successor — the D76.0 family's dead ICD10CM target upgrades
// to standard SNOMED CT 4278365, moving those claims to this collection's
// OMOP SNOMED CT concepts counterpart — 1 keeps its retired target demoted to
// quality 40 with effect omitted (M0529: poss_eq-only successor
// evidence, below the equivalence bar), and 1 is dropped to a no_match
// assessment because the invalid target contradicts the source term
// (S065, traumatic vs nontraumatic subdural hemorrhage).
translation-table "invalid-reason" version="1" source-column="invalid_reason" target-field="status|assessment|flag" {
    description "en" "Source invalid_reason values split by what they describe."
    entry "D" "status:inactive"
    entry "U" "status:retired"
    entry "manual_review_needed" "flag:needs-review"
    entry "false_positive" "flag:reported-false-positive"
    entry "no_valid_concept" "assessment:no_match"
    entry "icf_swedish_extension_no_target" "assessment:no_match"
    entry "no_ucum_equivalent" "assessment:no_match"
}
translation-table "source-provenance" version="1" source-column="mapping_provenance" target-field="imported" {
    description "en" "The source's mapping_provenance, kept as the imported label of each claim it produced."
    entry "athena" "athena" note="Athena Maps-to crosswalk, inherited"
    entry "automated" "automated"
    entry "curated" "curated"
    entry "manual" "manual"
    entry "rf2" drop=#true note="SNOMED CT-authored rows are not imported"
    entry "rf2-se" drop=#true note="SNOMED CT-authored rows are not imported"
}
// Fixes source target keys that name the wrong system, and maps raw
// source keys to their declared systems. The key is the source column
// (a bare key applies to every source); the value the system the
// target code really belongs to.
translation-table "target-key" version="1" source-column="maps_to key" target-field="target system" {
    description "en" "Source map-cell keys, per source vocabulary, translated to the system the target code belongs to. A bare key (no source prefix) applies to every source."
    entry "TLV_FBA/ICD-10" "ATC Y-codes" note="Y90 codes are ATC Y-codes, not ICD-10"
    entry "UNIT_SE/UCUM" "OMOP concepts" note="The values are official OMOP unit concept ids, not UCUM codes"
    entry "RX_NORM" "RxNorm" note="Declared code-only in drug/RXNORM/definitions.kdl"
    entry "MedDRA" "MedDRA" note="Declared code-only in _registry/external.kdl"
    entry "Orphanet" "Orphanet" note="Declared code-only in _registry/external.kdl"
    entry "ICD_10_SE/ICD-10-CM" "OMOP ICD-10-CM concepts" note="The cell values are OMOP concept ids for ICD-10-CM concepts, not ICD-10-CM codes"
    entry "ICD-10-CM" "ICD-10-CM" note="Declared code-only in _registry/external.kdl"
}
// OMOP custom concept ids: the reserved bands live beside the
// OMOP custom concepts system declaration in _registry/external.kdl (edges
// derived from the observed data). The stale
// omop-drug block that stood here covered 2100200000-2100299999, a
// range no binding in the tree ever fell inside.

// Census scheme `census@1` (deterministic; same tree -> same numbers).
// The importer emits _registry/census.kdl on every run under this
// scheme and nothing in it is authored by hand; the counts describe
// what the same run emitted. Counting rules:
//
//   - concepts: `concept` nodes declared in a system's concept files
//     (the data files whose context binds the system release).
//     `variant` and `code-alias` nodes are not concepts. Denominator
//     for the status and designation rows.
//   - inactive / retired: concepts whose effective status — their own
//     `status` or the file's `concepts.status` default — is
//     `inactive` / `retired`; every other concept is active.
//   - named / sv / en: concepts carrying at least one `name`
//     designation / one with locale `sv` / one with `en`. Synonyms and
//     variants do not count as designations.
//   - mappings: `mapping` nodes declared in a collection's mapping
//     files (the data files whose context binds the collection
//     version). Denominator for the kind rows and the assessed share.
//   - bindings: `omop-binding` nodes in the same files — an
//     identifier binding to an OMOP concept id, a different assertion
//     from a semantic mapping, counted apart and never given a kind.
//   - kind: a mapping's effective relationship — its own
//     `relationship` where spelled, else the uniform kind the
//     collection projects through its nested import.
//   - assessed: mappings carrying a derived `quality` or `effect`
//     property under rubric `mapping-quality@1`; every other mapping
//     is unassessed (not assessed is a statement about evidence, not
//     about correctness).
//   - tier: a mapping's confidence tier from its bound confidence
//     (census-tier rows, one per tier present): under scheme
//     `vocabmod-se-confidence@1` the calibrated tier scores map
//     0.87 -> H, 0.71 -> M, any lower score -> L; under scheme
//     `vocabmod-se-confidence-unassessable@1` every reason code is U.
//     A mapping carrying no confidence enters no tier, so the tier
//     rows sum to at most the collection's mappings.
